nodecode-scaleway is a rewrite of scaleway's scaleway/hermes-scaleway-provider:

  https://github.com/scaleway/hermes-scaleway-provider
  commit 685726e5d544f84384d619e979b7a93359bdec55
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Reda Maizate (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's one payload, `scaleway-provider/__init__.py`,
which registers a Hermes model provider named `scaleway` on base
https://api.scaleway.ai/v1 with the ambient SCW_SECRET_KEY, the
SCALEWAY_BASE_URL override, a curated `fallback_models` list led by
deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, `models_dev_id: scaleway` for context windows and
pricing, vision support, and the auxiliary model
mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct-2506. In Common Lisp that is a catalog row
(the curated ids, with the numbers from the models.dev `scaleway` row the
plugin's own test fixture records, in models.json), a credential hook that
reads SCW_SECRET_KEY and then SCALEWAY_API_KEY, and a section carrying the
base. `plugin.yaml`, `README.md` and the test suite around the payload were
read for what the profile means, not copied.

What was left out, and why: the `scw` alias, `ambient_credentials` and
`default_aux_model` have no per-provider counterpart in Nodecode — a
provider is named once, a model is picked once, and the auxiliary model is
the core's `general.auxiliary_model`, which the README says to set. The
plugin's live `/v1/models` catalog probe is Nodecode's own listing, asked
with the key from this cell's credential hook; the curated list is what the
picker offers, as in the original.
